fatigue syndrome patients.</article-title><source>Clin Exp Allergy</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>1450</fpage><lpage>1456</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14519154</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005805-Grans1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grans</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Evengard</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Gene expression profiling in the chronic fatigue syndrome.</article-title><source>J Intern Med</source><volume>258</volume><fpage>388</fpage><lpage>390</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16164580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005805-Kerr2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kerr</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Petty</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Burke</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gough</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fear</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Gene expression subtypes in patients with chronic fatigue syndrome/myalgic encephalomyelitis.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>197</volume><fpage>1171</fpage><lpage>1184</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18462164</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005805-Evengard1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evengard</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacks</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pedersen</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Sullivan</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The epidemiology of